{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/932866-dark-eras-the-grimms-seeming-2e","id":932866,"title":"Dark Eras - The Grimms Seeming (2E)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-17T04:50:22-07:00","id":932866,"title":"Dark Eras - The Grimms Seeming (2E)","content":"If you've picked up the latest Dark Eras book you'll find a slew of cool stuff for Changelings for both 1.5E and 2E, and they're fantastic. One thing caught my attention in particular and this is in the Grimm section of the book, towards the end it gives details of a new Seeming, the Grimms.<br /> <br /> They are the Storytale Changelings, they are your little Red Riding Hoods and your Rapunzels, the Redcap, when they are not taking a role they are a myriad of pages and swirls of ink. When they are playing a role, they appear as the character that suits the situation. An example provided is that if a man is trapped in a tower in need of rescue, he will take on the features of the iconic Rapunzel. <br /> <br /> Unfortunately, they don't particularly have any examples of characters to go along with this, of how each Kith might work, so I thought it'd be a good plan to put it up here, maybe some examples or ideas people might have.<br /> <br /> The Hunterheart, depending on her mark at the time, becomes the Big Bad Wolf or The Huntsman. When she is tracking someone compared to when she is fighting a bigger creature from the Hedge. The whole time, the words and phrases of various hunters dance around their skin.<br /> <br /> A Coldscale takes on a manipulative tone and is seen as a snake, like Kaa from the Junglebook, as small whispers are written across his scales, but when it comes to overthrowing a tyrannical figure of the Freehold, the Crocodile from Peter Pan comes into fruition. <br /> <br /> An Earthbones seems to look a bit like The Cave of Wonders as a humanoid as he keeps valuables safe and hidden.<br /> <br /> How do people feel about this new Seeming? Will it appear in your games in the future?<br /> <br /> Additionally, a question I do have is will we get more information on the Seeming in the 2E Changeling sourcebooks coming out? For example the Seeming Bonuses for the contracts, alongside the 8th Seeming coming in the Hedge?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1740-soirgriffe","name":"Soirgriffe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-17T06:36:42-07:00","id":932881,"title":"","content":"Some of the homebrew kiths in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e\">this thread</a> have some examples using the Grimm seeming.<br /> <br /> I also remember doing a few Seeming clauses for them in another thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-17T06:56:27-07:00","id":932886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Soirgriffe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/932866-dark-eras-the-grimms-seeming-2e#post932866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you've picked up the latest Dark Eras book you'll find a slew of cool stuff for Changelings for both 1.5E and 2E, and they're fantastic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why, thank you!<br /> <br /> I didn't write the Seeming, I wrote the chapter's Inspirational media Section, What Has Come Before, Contracts and the Companions of the Resigned. Mina Young wrote the Seeming. <br /> <br /> I love it, personally, but I haven't had the chance to use it yet in a game. I'm also not working on the other Changeling books, so I can't comment as to whether or not they will appear (though, I can say and I believe it's been said that they are still a Seeming in the present. That is to say, they're intended to remain a thing, they're not just a Seeming of the past).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-17T21:34:12-07:00","id":933252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Soirgriffe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/932866-dark-eras-the-grimms-seeming-2e#post932866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you've picked up the latest Dark Eras book you'll find a slew of cool stuff for Changelings for both 1.5E and 2E, and they're fantastic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed; there was loads of material in the book I loved, particularly the expansions to Changeling history, and the examples of the entitlements Changeling 2e could offer. Lovely range to it all.<br /> <br /> I'm currently making my own freehold and, in preparation for a potential game, I've made one of the courts (Paint) recently go through a change in rulers. Though the new one is an Elemental Ifrit/Gristlegrinder, the previous one is both a Grimm and still active in court duties, alongside his Fae Touched wife (she is also a Grimm, having picked up the Seeming when she met her husband in the Hedge and they made their way out together). He's a Chatelaine, and the mask reference I have for him is of Alex Macqueen, with his wife's reference being Michelle Gomez - there's a pretty nerdy joke in there, but I couldn't resist. The stuff I have planned for them is pretty dark though...hope I end up using the material somewhere.<br /> <br /> I'm also making custom contracts for the courts, though thus far only the Paint court has had any real progress, and two of the contracts have Grimm Seeming bonuses. It's quite fun having yet another seeming to work with, though it does make it a bit crowded trying to make at least one bonus for each Seeming in five contracts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5803,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","user":"Taidragon","date":". 07-18-2016, 12:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-17T22:17:09-07:00","id":933266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/932866-dark-eras-the-grimms-seeming-2e?p=933252#post933252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Agreed; there was loads of material in the book I loved, particularly the expansions to Changeling history, and the examples of the entitlements Changeling 2e could offer. Lovely range to it all.<br /> <br /> I'm currently making my own freehold and, in preparation for a potential game, I've made one of the courts (Paint) recently go through a change in rulers. Though the new one is an Elemental Ifrit/Gristlegrinder, the previous one is both a Grimm and still active in court duties, alongside his Fae Touched wife (she is also a Grimm, having picked up the Seeming when she met her husband in the Hedge and they made their way out together). He's a Chatelaine, and the mask reference I have for him is of Alex Macqueen, with his wife's reference being Michelle Gomez - there's a pretty nerdy joke in there, but I couldn't resist. The stuff I have planned for them is pretty dark though...hope I end up using the material somewhere.<br /> <br /> I'm also making custom contracts for the courts, though thus far only the Paint court has had any real progress, and two of the contracts have Grimm Seeming bonuses. It's quite fun having yet another seeming to work with, though it does make it a bit crowded trying to make at least one bonus for each Seeming in five contracts.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Please let me know if you end up working with the Companions at all!<br /> <br /> And if you like my work with children, stay tuned for the Dark Eras Companion and the Beast Ready-Made PCs ^_^.<br /> <br /> Can't say anything more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-17T22:36:52-07:00","id":933273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hm8453a</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/932866-dark-eras-the-grimms-seeming-2e?p=933266#post933266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Please let me know if you end up working with the Companions at all!<br /> <br /> And if you like my work with children, stay tuned for the Dark Eras Companion and the Beast Ready-Made PCs ^_^.<br /> <br /> Can't say anything more.</div> </div> </div> </div>That I shall~<br /> <br /> And you have me riveted for what is to come. o3o<br /> <br /> Edit: ...I just realized I got Chatelaine and Chirurgeon mixed up. The joke I mentioned above doesn't quite work as well for someone who's unendingly polite...unless it's Peter Davison's era...I do believe an idea has come about...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5803,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","user":"Taidragon","date":". 07-18-2016, 03:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T20:56:21-07:00","id":939940,"title":"","content":"Semi-related, I just watched the horror anthology &quot;Holidays&quot; at Matt McFarland's urging, and the Easter segment has a Grimm. I think. My interpretation.<br /> <br /> Also, it's fucked, so be prepared if you're going to watch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":3093,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","user":"hm8453a","date":". 07-30-2016, 12:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}